              "text": "**Mundra Port** is the **largest commercial, container, and private port in India**. \n\nHere is a breakdown of its location, ownership, and significance:\n\n### 1. Location\n* **Where:** It is located on the northern shores of the **Gulf of Kutch** near the town of Mundra, in the Kutch district of **Gujarat, India**. \n* **Strategic Advantage:** Its western coast location makes it a critical maritime gateway for trade routes heading to and from the Middle East, Europe, Africa, and the Americas.\n\n### 2. Ownership and Management\n* Mundra is a **private port** developed and operated by **Adani Ports and Special Economic Zone Limited (APSEZ)**, the flagship port operator of the Indian multinational conglomerate, the **Adani Group**. \n* Incorporated in 1998, it was India's first major private port and serves as the crown jewel of APSEZ's port portfolio.\n\n### 3. Scale and Capacity\n* **Major Trade Hub:** The port handles roughly **11% of India's total maritime cargo** and about **33% (one-third) of India\u2019s container traffic**. \n* **Cargo Volumes:** It handles well over 150 million metric tonnes (MMT) of cargo annually, having recently made history by crossing the 200 MMT mark in a single fiscal year.\n* **Deep-Water Port:** It is a deep-draft, all-weather port with a natural depth of up to 15\u201316 meters. This allows it to accommodate some of the world's largest cargo and container vessels (such as the giant container ship *MSC Anna*, which docked there in 2024).\n\n### 4. Key Facilities & Infrastructure\n* **Terminals:** The port features multiple specialized terminals handling diverse cargo, including dry bulk, liquid cargo, crude oil, and automobiles. It has five container terminals with 12 berths.\n* **Coal Terminal:** It is home to the world's largest import coal terminal.\n* **Special Economic Zone (SEZ):** The port is integrated with India's largest port-based multi-product Special Economic Zone (SEZ), making it a massive hub for manufacturing, industrial development, and logistics.",
